Hi,

We are running DECSystem 5400 with two CXY08 serial adapters as the
Finnish EUnet backbone.  We have both ISDN adaptors and V.32 modems
(US Robotics DS) connected to the serial ports, most of them are
configured at 19.2kbps.

Currently we are using Ultrix 3.1A without any major problem, however
we would be greatly interested to upgrade to the newer Ultrix version.

We have tried to upgrade to Ultrix 4.0, but we had serious problems with
the serial ports.  After booting the system everything works just
fine, however ofter couple of hours the serial lines stop working one
by one.  Some of the modem signals work, ie. modems are still
answering, however getty will not wake up to the incoming calls.  This
seems to be problem on the Ultrix side because the ISDN lines with
special getty continue to work.

We have also tried Ultrix 4.1, but we were unable to test the serial
ports because I had problems with getting Sendmail 5.64 + IDA 1.3.1 to
work correctly.  The serial ports worked at least for a short time.

We cannot stay with the Ultrix 3.1 forever, so I would like to get in
touch with DEC users familiar with the CXY08 cards and similar
equipment.  Also I would like to know if others have got CXY08's to
work with Ultrix 4.0/4.1 or are having similar problems.

Thanks!

Regards,
	Petri Ojala
